# Commercial S12.1 durable recovery and fresh-evidence diagnosis

- Scope: final pre-freeze review of detached rollback, interrupted controller,
  and pre-existing-unit acceptance.
- Findings:
  - detached rollback restored HEAD but not the independently advanced named
    release branch;
  - a SIGKILL/reboot after the attempt marker had no rollback-only entrypoint;
  - `systemctl start` did not first prove the unit inactive or distinguish new
    acceptance evidence from stale success files.
- Corrections:
  - backup records and rollback verifies exact `main`/`control-main` tips in
    addition to HEAD posture;
  - `recover` loads the root-private restore index and runs rollback only,
    without a second acceptance start;
  - preflight requires `inactive/dead`; prior evidence is backed up and removed;
    newly created root-private evidence must be timestamped within this attempt.
- Boundaries: no second deploy, no gate bypass, no secret output, no provider or
  Production expansion, and no server attempt has yet occurred.
